  <p>
    Hi, I’m Jorge Guzman. I graduated from Georgia Gwinnett College
    with a B.S. in Applied Mathematics in December 2025. My interests
    include topology, algebra, dynamical systems, and AI.
  </p>

  <p>
    I enjoy working through proofs, exploring ideas with code, and
    finding explanations that make difficult mathematics easier to
    understand. My undergraduate work included group theory,
    topological data analysis, and mathematical modeling.
  </p>

  <p>
    Altered Chain is where I share what I’m learning and building.
    You’ll find mathematical explanations, computational experiments,
    and notes on topics that catch my curiosity. I’m also exploring
    how tools like Lean and AI can support mathematical understanding.
  </p>

  <p>
    Outside mathematics, I enjoy tennis, films, and science fiction.
    You can explore my <a href="/blog/">blog</a> and
    <a href="/projects/">projects</a>, or reach out through
    <a href="https://github.com/360Jorge">GitHub</a> or
